  "goodToKnow": "Die Lyrik is poetry as a literary genre, alongside Epik (narrative) and Dramatik (drama) in German school terminology. It's a false friend: song lyrics are der Songtext or Liedtext. Der Lyriker (die Lyrikerin) is a poet, and lyrisch means lyrical or poetic. Famous German Lyriker include Goethe, Heine, Rilke and Ingeborg Bachmann; schoolchildren often learn a poem by heart, auswendig lernen. The y is pronounced like ü: LÜ-rik."
